ke P: f7–f5 immediately create a weakness and overextend before the rook is ready; P: c5–c4 leaves a hole on d4 and doesn’t improve piece activity; K: d8–c7 avoids danger but wastes a tempo. R: h8–f8 is the most flexible and constructive move.\n\nAnswer: R: h8-f8'}
